{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"today we're going to work on making this package not so damn annoying, specifically the secret/redaction system that i swear to god becomes a whole chore every single time i do anything inside this project or ../turnbridge. make us a new worktree in a new ../conversation-ledger-worktrees/ folder. here's the rundown of all my thoughts about the issue:\n- having to jump out of my coding agent CLI every time cledger recognizes a secret is a major workflow breaker\n- the .txt files for letting the human inspect the issue are not very easy to read. i'd almost prefer maybe a TUI with the potential secret color coded where i can scroll through the conversation history rather than being restricted to x characters on either side of the secret\n- i'm suggesting a lot of stuff right now but please don't jump to implementing any of it naively. we need to make sure whatever we end up doing meshes well with the core thesis/requirements of the project and think about what is in-scope today vs deferred to later\n- i think the system has some sort of fundamental capturing flaw causing it to either be overly sensitive or something. or at the very least the llms i'm working with are maybe constantly adding new fake-secrets into the test fixtures or something only to have them need to get manually added to the allow-list later. we need some sort of a system to ensure that all secret-like test-fixtures get added to the approval system immediately upon their creation rather than at the end of that PR attempting to push and merge.\n- i think maybe we need to make clear to the users (kinda meaning me) what exactly is and is not the expectation of somebody using this project in terms of security. at a certain point our security/redaction systems can't find everything, so we need to clarify in the config and whatnot that they should be properly setting permissions on secrets files such that LLMs can't read them, not pasting their secrets into LLM CLIs, etc\n- we need to go through and clarify the point at which we actually ensure security, which i think is _before_ push, and, whatever that is, make sure our code actually aligns with it\n- oh and this issue is active rn we need to also fix a current set of cledger push issue instances\n- any other ideas for how to make this process feel smoother on my end?","type":"text"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"redaction-ux","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger-worktrees/redaction-ux","head":"fb4df15a7bdebc38ca45aa5ad908b0fcb411d13c","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:b8bc0200-5312-42a4-9c54-a116d8d4a925","seq":9},"id":"ev1-b4e36db120427ea0739dd85f7b8ec49dbbf992fe58b06babe592c462185221e8","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-12T01:15:03.572Z","producer":{"session_id":"b8bc0200-5312-42a4-9c54-a116d8d4a925","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.228","tool":"cledger","version":"0.20.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":"today we're going to work on making this package not so damn annoying, specifically the secret/redaction system that i swear to god becomes a whole chore every single time i do anything inside this project or ../turnbridge. make us a new worktree in a new ../conversation-ledger-worktrees/ folder. here's the rundown of all my thoughts about the issue:\n- having to jump out of my coding agent CLI every time cledger recognizes a secret is a major workflow breaker\n- the .txt files for letting the human inspect the issue are not very easy to read. i'd almost prefer maybe a TUI with the potential secret color coded where i can scroll through the conversation history rather than being restricted to x characters on either side of the secret\n- i'm suggesting a lot