{"actor":{"id":"claude-fable-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_01UBJn2GD6DLTc3K16jxVaVZ","input":{"command":"git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nRedaction review UX: grouped reports, cledger review, allowlist tiers, fixture markers (0.21.0)\n\nThe scan gate was doing its job and losing the user anyway: 153 finding\nsites that were really 11 decisions, a review flow that meant leaving the\nagent CLI to read a .txt file and hand-type a regex of the secret just\nread, per-repo allowlists that made every downstream repo re-review spans\na human already cleared, and fixture-writing agents seeding new findings\nwith every fake credential they typed.\n\nIn scope here:\n- Reports group by fingerprint: one block per distinct span, sites and\n  event coordinates beneath. Scan stdout keeps one-line-per-site for CI.\n- `cledger review`: interactive triage, humans only (agent-session refusal\n  plus hard TTY requirement, no --force). One screen per span, match\n  highlighted in context; allow here / allow globally / redact / skip.\n  Redaction escapes the span into a literal pattern itself.\n- Allowlist tiers, unioned at scan time: per-repo file, per-user file\n  (`allow --global`), and `scan.allowFingerprints` in .cledger.json so a\n  repo can commit its own known false positives.\n- Uppercase fixture markers (FAKE/EXAMPLE/PLACEHOLDER/DUMMY/NOTREAL/\n  TESTONLY) exempt scan-tier heuristic matches; capture-tier formats\n  deliberately ignore markers. CLAUDE.md teaches agents the convention so\n  fixtures never enter the queue at all.\n- Enforcement-point audit fixes: config sections now merge per-key\n  (the documented fails-open replacement bug), and inAgentSession knows\n  the opencode/gemini/qwen markers, not just Claude/Codex.\n- README: explicit \"what cledger does and does not protect\" expectations;\n  the enforced guarantee is the pre-push gate, everything else is\n  harm reduction.\n\nConsidered and deferred, recorded in the roadmap